    "text": "<p>Using monochromatic light of wavelength <math> <mrow> <mi>&#955;</mi> </mrow> </math>,&nbsp;an experimentalist sets up the Young&#39;s double slit experiment in three ways as shown.<br />If she observes that <math> <mrow> <mi></mi><mi></mi><mi></mi><mi></mi><mi></mi><mi></mi><mi></mi><mi>y</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo> <mo>=</mo> <msup> <mi>&#946;</mi> <mo>&#8242;</mo> </msup> </mrow> </math>,&nbsp;the wavelength of light used is :<br /><br />&nbsp; <u><strong><img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\qt0137_cb4560baf3e4.jpg\" style=\"width: 250px; height: 144px;\" /></strong></u> <img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\qt0137_7b019aff2e65.jpg\" style=\"width: 250px; height: 175px;\" /> <img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\qt0137_2133fedf81bc.jpg\" style=\"width: 250px; height: 146px;\" /></p>"
